    "type": "body_plan", "id": "humanoid", "name": "humanoid",
    "//": [
      "weight: share of random hits. hit_penalty: called-shot penalty.",
      "cripple_at / fracture_at / destroy_at: fractions of max HP of injury to that part.",
      "fracture_at only applies to damage types with 'fractures' (blunt force).",
      "destroy_at applies to 'dismembers' damage types, or to any type if the part is an 'organ'.",
      "internal: injuries of at least at x HP start internal bleeding (bleed x injury/HP %/s) that won't clot.",
      "brain: injuries add brain damage (brain_damage x injury/HP); 100 total is death.",
      "by_type: per-damage-type overrides of the part's fields (texts, sever_item, fracture_status...).",
      "A part is wrenchable in a hold if it has a by_type entry for 'wrench'. dr.wrench is how hard the joint resists.",
      "sever_item: the item left behind when the part comes off (sever_name names it: \"Bob's head\").",
      "fracture_status: a status applied when the part breaks (a snapped neck: broken_neck).",
      "concussion: a hard enough hit here can knock you out (the head). Anywhere else a big hit only knocks you down.",
      "deep: organ destruction here counts only the part of each wound that reaches deep (damage type 'depth': a slash is 0.25, a stab 1).",
      "grab: can be grabbed in a hold (at hit_penalty). choke: a grip on it can choke and strangle, and silences them.",
      "dr.squeeze: how well it holds up to being crushed in a grip (a bear hug, a crushing handshake).",
      "organs: what's under a part. A wound whose deep injury reaches the damage type's organ_at (x HP) hits one of them, by weight ('miss': nothing vital): bleed (internal %/s, scaled by how deep), external_bleed, status (with chance; 'effect' / 'else' say what it did).",
      "fracture_punctures: once this part is broken (ribs), another heavy blunt blow to it (or a part 'under' it) may drive a bone into one of these organs (chance).",
      "dislocate_at: a wound this big (x HP) from a damage type with 'dislocates' (a chance) can put the joint out: useless and agony until someone resets it (first aid, a splint)."
    ],
